null, "end_idx": 1170, "fff_metadata": null, "id": "file_00000000dc7482098c64935c217ed37b", "input_pointer": {"file_index": 0, "line_range_end": 85, "line_range_start": 81, "message_id": "3cad0b9c-c2aa-475e-bf13-c79aab0d62df", "message_index": 0}, "library_artifact_type": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_0ff357eaf20c819193c84b3d7d5efef6", "matched_text": "fileciteturn0file0L81-L85", "medical_file_reference": {"authors_display": null, "doi": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "publication_year": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null}, "name": "Pasted text.txt", "page_range_end": null, "page_range_start": null, "snippet": "14. MINIMUM REVERSIBLE RECOVERY PLAN (not executed)\nONE change: in handle_command, make single-word commands fire only on exact-utterance equality (reuse the 9/24 standalone mechanism); keep multi-word deliberate phrases (copy that, paste it, go to luce, focus number N, delete word…) on leading-match. Impact: deliberate short commands still work when said alone; dictation openings type.\nTest: pytest + self-test + add cases (Right, … types, Up in the morning types, Who is calling types). Clean single-instance restart.", "source": "my_files", "start_idx": 1141, "type": "file"}, {"alt": null, "api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "cloud_doc_url": null, "connector_id": null, "drug_file_reference": null, "end_idx": 1483, "fff_metadata": null, "id": "file_00000000dc7482098c64935c217ed37b", "input_pointer": {"file_index": 0, "line_range_end": 78, "line_range_start": 72, "message_id": "3cad0b9c-c2aa-475e-bf13-c79aab0d62df", "message_index": 0}, "library_artifact_type": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_0ff357eaf20c819193c84b3d7d5efef6", "matched_text": "fileciteturn0file0L72-L78", "medical_file_reference": {"authors_display": null, "doi": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "publication_year": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null}, "name": "Pasted text.txt", "page_range_end": null, "page_range_start": null, "snippet": "12. OPTIMIZATION FINDINGS\nOptimization\tOld → New\tBenefit\tObserved side effect\tRegression risk\nVAD-lite gate (9/23)\talways-stream → gate silence\tcost/CPU/billing\tnone confirmed\tquiet-speech clip (low)\n...", "source": "my_files", "start_idx": 1454, "type": "file"}, {"alt": null, "api_tool_source": "files/context_stuff", "cloud_doc_url": null, "connector_id": null, "drug_file_reference": null, "end_idx": 2063, "fff_metadata": null, "id": "file_00000000dc7482098c64935c217ed37b", "input_pointer": {"file_index": 0, "line_range_end": 15, "line_range_start": 4, "message_id": "3cad0b9c-c2aa-475e-bf13-c79aab0d62df", "message_index": 0}, "library_artifact_type": null, "library_file_id": "libfile_0ff357eaf20c819193c84b3d7d5efef6", "matched_text": "fileciteturn0file0L4-L15", "medical_file_reference": {"authors_display": null, "doi": null, "journal_homepage_url": null, "journal_name": null, "publication_year": null, "source_icon_url": null, "source_label": null, "source_url": null}, "name": "Pasted text.txt", "page_range_end": null, "page_range_start": null, "snippet": "2. LIVE PROJECT / ESTATE MAP\nLIVE:      C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\voice-bridge        (only live copy)\nLaunchers: Desktop\\VoiceBridge.lnk  -> .venv\\Scripts\\pythonw.exe -m src.voice_bridge  (workdir voice-bridge)", "source": "my_files", "start_idx": 2035, "type": "file"}], "conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible": true, "cot_version": "v5", "default_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "finish_details": {"stop_tokens": [200002], "type": "stop"}, "gizmo_id": "g-p-6ab41b7c2620819187c626358eeb8a48", "is_complete": true, "message_type": "next", "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "model_switcher_deny": [], "parent_id": "819dfb1f-4c1e-48af-a3ad-3eef0e8cc2b9", "request_id": "9e07f33c-3824-46b2-8d51-b78529636b82", "resolved_model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "search_result_groups": [], "story_events": [], "thinking_effort": "standard", "turn_exchange_id": "1fa937eb-4f04-401c-b14e-5de1778fc771", "working_turn_id": "1fa937eb-4f04-401c-b14e-5de1778fc771"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790283597.924155, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "user"}, "channel": null, "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["yes i approve give me surgica l fuix for nico"]}, "create_time": 1790283638.212, "end_turn": null, "id": "c406901f-057c-46a6-a284-36fa5986c6c0", "metadata": {"can_save": false, "message_source": null, "request_id": "ec77cae0-0e2f-4c38-9a1e-6c5ed96fdba0", "selected_sources": [], "serialization_metadata": {"custom_symbol_offsets": []}, "turn_exchange_id": "a972a55d-29b0-494e-a97d-301e15c04e81", "working_turn_id": "a972a55d-29b0-494e-a97d-301e15c04e81"}, "recipient": "all", "status": "finished_successfully", "update_time": 1790283689.688285, "weight": 1}, {"author": {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Absolutely. This should be a **tight Nico implementation order**: one surgical routing fix, one command-language change, tests, restart, verification. No cleanup, no refactor, no provider work.\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" id=\"73194\" title=\"Nico — VoiceBridge Surgical Regression Fix\"}\n# GCE VOICEBRIDGE — NICO SURGICAL FIX ORDER\n\n**DATE:** 2026-09-24  \n**AUTHORITY:** Don  \n**SEAT:** Nico — Implementation / Builder  \n**SOURCE:** Luce regression recon  \n**MODE:** SURGICAL CORRECTION ONLY  \n**PROJECT:** `C:\\Users\\Dekan AI Brother\\GCE_DON\\voice-bridge`\n\n---\n\n# 0. AUTHORIZED DECISIONS\n\nDon approves both corrective decisions identified by Luce:\n\n1. **Single-word commands must execute only when the entire utterance equals the command.**\n2. **Bare `sleep` / `wake up` are no longer acceptable global control commands.**\n\nReplace the pause/resume language with deliberate phrases:\n\n```text\nstop listening\nstart listening\n```\n\nThese should require exact-utterance matching.\n\nDo not preserve bare `sleep` or bare `wake up` as active aliases.\n\n---\n\n# 1. OBJECTIVE\n\nCorrect the command-vs-dictation boundary without changing the healthy upstream VoiceBridge pipeline.\n\nVerified healthy components include:\n\n```text\nmicrophone capture\n→ AssemblyAI streaming STT\n→ final transcript\n→ queue / dispatcher\n→ corrections\n```\n\nThe verified failure boundary is:\n\n```text\nsrc/voice_commands.py\nhandle_command()\n```\n\nwith integration through:\n\n```text\nsrc/voice_bridge.py\ncontinuous dictation path\n```\n\nThe current parser allows single-word commands to match the beginning of ordinary dictation, causing destructive keyboard actions.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\n\"Right, if you need me...\"\n→ RIGHT ARROW\n\n\"Save the document...\"\n→ CTRL+S\n\n\"Copy the notes...\"\n→ CTRL+C\n```\n\nThis must stop.\n\n---\n\n# 2. HARD SCOPE BOUNDARY\n\nDo **not** modify:\n\n- AssemblyAI provider logic\n- capture pipeline\n- WebSocket handling\n- VAD implementation\n- silence threshold\n- transcript finalization\n- transcription correction table unless required by a failing test directly related to this fix\n- intent audit system\n- UI\n- TTS\n- QueuePanel\n- Cockpit\n- dependency versions\n- `.env`\n- project folder structure\n- archive copies\n- documentation cleanup\n- unrelated dead configuration\n\nDo not refactor the command system generally.\n\nThis is a routing-boundary patch only.\n\n---\n\n# 3. CURRENT DEFECT\n\nLuce verified that `handle_command()` currently permits single-word commands to behave like leading-prefix commands.\n\nConceptually, the current behavior is equivalent to:\n\n```python\nif text starts with \"right\":\n    execute RIGHT\n```\n\nThat is incorrect for continuous dictation.\n\nThe desired behavior is:\n\n```python\nif normalized utterance == \"right\":\n    execute RIGHT\nelse:\n    treat as dictation\n```\n\nThis rule applies to **single-word command triggers**.\n\n---\n\n# 4. IMPLEMENTATION RULE\n\n## A. SINGLE-WORD COMMANDS\n\nFor every command whose trigger is exactly one lexical word, require **exact normalized utterance equality**.\n\nExamples include the currently verified collision family:\n\n```text\nright\nleft\nup\ndown\nenter\nsend\nspace\nsave\ncopy\nquote\nwho\n```\n\nAlso inspect the current command registry/parser for **all other single-word triggers** and apply the same rule consistently.\n\nDo not patch only the eleven reproduced examples if more single-token commands exist.\n\nNormalization may preserve the project's existing behavior for:\n\n- case\n- surrounding whitespace\n- terminal punctuation\n\nExample:\n\n```text\n\"Right\"\n\"right\"\n\"RIGHT.\"\n```\n\nmay all resolve to the command `right`.\n\nBut:\n\n```text\n\"Right, if you need me\"\n\"right now\"\n\"right side\"\n```\n\nmust **not** execute the command.\n\nThey must remain dictation.\n\n---\n\n# 5. MULTI-WORD COMMANDS\n\nDo not indiscriminately convert all command parsing to exact equality.\n\nExisting deliberate multi-word commands may retain current matching semantics where appropriate.\n\nExamples mentioned in recon include constructs such as:\n\n```text\ncopy that\npaste it\ngo to luce\nfocus number N\ndelete word ...\n```\n\nPreserve those unless an existing test demonstrates otherwise.\n\nThe surgical distinction is:\n\n```text\nONE-WORD TRIGGER\n→ exact utterance only\n\nDELIBERATE MULTI-WORD COMMAND\n→ preserve existing parser behavior\n```\n\n---\n\n# 6. PAUSE / RESUME CHANGE\n\nRemove active command recognition for:\n\n```text\nsleep\nwake up\n```\n\nDo not leave hidden aliases that can still cause the same failure.\n\nReplace with:\n\n```text\nstop listening\nstart listening\n```\n\nBoth commands must use exact normalized utterance equality.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\n\"stop listening\"\n→ pause bridge\n\n\"stop listening.\"\n→ pause bridge\n\n\"we should stop listening to that\"\n→ dictation\n\n\"start listening\"\n→ resume bridge\n\n\"start listening tomorrow\"\n→ dictation\n```\n\nA dictated standalone:\n\n```text\n\"Sleep.\"\n```\n\nmust now type as normal dictation.\n\nIt must never set:\n\n```python\nself.paused = True\n```\n\n---\n\n# 7. PAUSED-STATE SAFETY\n\nReview the paused path in `voice_bridge.py`.\n\nThe intended state machine is:\n\n```text\nACTIVE\n  └─ exact \"stop listening\"\n        ↓\nPAUSED\n\nPAUSED\n  ├─ exact \"start listening\"\n  │      ↓\n  │    ACTIVE\n  │\n  └─ everything else\n         → ignored while paused\n```\n\nDo not add fuzzy matching.\n\nDo not allow:\n\n```text\nstart\nlistening\nwake\nwake up\nresume\n```\n\nunless they are already independently required by current authoritative behavior.\n\nFor this slice, `start listening` is the authorized resume phrase.\n\n---\n\n# 8. REQUIRED TESTS\n\nAdd regression tests before declaring success.\n\nAt minimum cover:\n\n## A. single-word command still works alone\n\n```text\n\"Right\"          → RIGHT command\n\"Left\"           → LEFT command\n\"Up\"             → UP command\n\"Down\"           → DOWN command\n\"Enter\"          → ENTER command\n\"Save\"           → SAVE command\n\"Copy\"           → COPY command\n```\n\n## B. command word at beginning of dictation does NOT fire\n\n```text\n\"Right, if you need me\"      → type text\n\"Up in the morning\"          → type text\n\"Down the street\"            → type text\n\"Left on the shelf\"          → type text\n\"Enter the building\"         → type text\n\"Send the file\"              → type text\n\"Space is big\"               → type text\n\"Save the document\"          → type text\n\"Copy the notes\"             → type text\n\"Quote from the document\"    → type text\n\"Who is calling\"             → type text\n```\n\nThese are Luce's verified collision cases and must become permanent regression coverage.\n\n## C. pause/resume\n\n```text\n\"stop listening\"             → pause\n\"stop listening.\"            → pause\n\"we should stop listening\"   → type text\n\n\"start listening\"            → resume\n\"start listening.\"           → resume\n\"start listening tomorrow\"   → type text\n```\n\n## D. former collisions\n\n```text\n\"Sleep.\"                     → type text\n\"sleep\"                      → type text\n\"Wake up.\"                   → type text unless otherwise part of normal dictation handling\n```\n\nNo pause/resume action may occur.\n\n---\n\n# 9. PRESERVE EXISTING TESTS\n\nRun the complete suite.\n\nCurrent Luce baseline:\n\n```text\npytest tests/\n81 passed\n\n--self-test\n11/11 OK\n```\n\nDo not accept a patch that fixes the new regression tests while breaking existing behavior.\n\nRequired final result:\n\n```text\nexisting tests: PASS\nnew regression tests: PASS\nself-test: PASS\n```\n\nIf counts increase because new tests were added, report both old and new totals.\n\n---\n\n# 10. MANUAL SMOKE TEST\n\nAfter automated tests pass, perform a **clean single-instance restart** using the current authorized launcher/runtime.\n\nVerify there is only one VoiceBridge runtime instance, accounting for the existing venv shim/interpreter process relationship.\n\nThen manually test at least:\n\n```text\nRight.\nRight, this is a normal sentence.\n\nSave.\nSave the document for later.\n\nCopy.\nCopy the notes over here.\n\nSleep.\nstop listening\nstart listening\n\nWho.\nWho is calling me?\n```\n\nRecord:\n\n```text\nUTTERANCE\nEXPECTED\nACTUAL\nPASS/FAIL\n```\n\nDo not rely only on unit tests.\n\n---\n\n# 11. LOG VERIFICATION\n\nAfter smoke test, inspect:\n\n```text\nintent_audit.log\nbridge.log\n```\n\nConfirm:\n\n### command utterance\n\n```text\nRight.\n```\n\nshows command execution.\n\n### dictation utterance\n\n```text\nRight, this is a normal sentence.\n```\n\nshows dictation/type path and **not**:\n\n```text\ncommand: right\n```\n\n### former pause collision\n\n```text\nSleep.\n```\n\nmust not show a pause transition.\n\n### new pause phrase\n\n```text\nstop listening\n```\n\nmust show pause.\n\n### new resume phrase\n\n```text\nstart listening\n```\n\nmust show resume.\n\nIf `bridge.log` remains stale as Luce observed, report that separately.\n\nDo not widen this fix to repair logging unless logging blocks verification.\n\n---\n\n# 12. CHANGE MINIMIZATION\n\nPrefer the smallest implementation that creates one clear distinction inside or immediately around `handle_command()`:\n\n```text\nsingle-token command\n→ exact normalized equality\n\nmulti-token command\n→ existing behavior\n```\n\nAvoid copying command lists into multiple places if the parser can derive token count from existing command definitions.\n\nIf a helper is necessary, keep it narrow and testable.\n\nExample conceptual helper:\n\n```python\ndef command_matches(trigger, utterance):\n    if trigger_is_single_word(trigger):\n        return utterance == trigger\n    return existing_match_behavior(trigger, utterance)\n```\n\nThis is conceptual only.\n\nUse the project's current architecture rather than forcing this exact implementation.\n\n---\n\n# 13. DO NOT CLEAN WHILE HERE\n\nLuce separately identified:\n\n- stale Deepgram-era docs\n- README drift\n- dead config\n- `.lnk.backup`\n- empty archive folder\n- uncommitted working tree\n\nDo **not** touch those in this implementation slice.\n\nThey belong to later cleanup.\n\n---\n\n# 14. VERSION CONTROL SAFETY\n\nThe live AssemblyAI / continuous implementation is currently largely uncommitted.\n\nBefore modifying code:\n\n1. capture `git status`\n2. capture `git diff`\n3. preserve the existing working state\n4. do not overwrite unrelated uncommitted changes\n\nAfter successful verification, return the exact files changed and diff summary.\n\nDo not perform a broad commit containing unrelated work.\n\nIf creating a commit is appropriate under the current local workflow, keep it surgical.\n\nSuggested semantic scope:\n\n```text\nfix(voicebridge): prevent single-word command collisions in dictation\n```\n\nBut do not commit automatically if current project governance requires Don review first.\n\n---\n\n# 15. REQUIRED NICO RETURN\n\nReturn:\n\n```text\nGCE VOICEBRIDGE — NICO SURGICAL FIX RETURN\n\n1. STATUS\n2. PRE-CHANGE GIT STATE\n3. ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED\n4. FILES CHANGED\n5. EXACT BEHAVIOR CHANGE\n6. PAUSE/RESUME CHANGE\n7. TESTS ADDED\n8. FULL TEST RESULTS\n9. SELF-TEST RESULT\n10. MANUAL SMOKE RESULTS\n11. LOG VERIFICATION\n12. REMAINING ISSUES\n13. DIFF SUMMARY\n14. SAFE FOR LUCE RE-VERIFICATION\n```\n\nFinish with:\n\n```text\nNICO VERDICT\n\nSINGLE-WORD COLLISION FIXED:\n[YES / NO]\n\nBARE SLEEP COLLISION REMOVED:\n[YES / NO]\n\nNEW PAUSE PHRASE:\nstop listening\n\nNEW RESUME PHRASE:\nstart listening\n\nFULL TEST SUITE:\n<PASS/FAIL + count>\n\nSELF-TEST:\n<PASS/FAIL + count>\n\nLIVE SMOKE:\n<PASS/FAIL>\n\nUNRELATED CHANGES MADE:\n[NO / list]\n\nSAFE FOR LUCE:\n[YES / NO]\n\nCONFIDENCE:\n<0-100%>\n```\n\n---\n\n# 16. STOP CONDITION\n\nIf the requested fix requires modification outside the command-routing boundary, stop and report why before widening scope.\n\nDo not redesign VoiceBridge.\n\nDo not optimize it further.\n\n**Repair the proven collision, prove the repair, and hand it back to Luce.**\n:::\n\nOnce Nico returns, I’d route it **straight back to Luce for adversarial re-verification**, specifically trying to break command-vs-dictation again rather than just confirming Nico’s happy-path tests."]}, "create_time": 1790283640.135053, "end_turn": true, "id": "3fbe8f37-5826-45e1-b37a-773c29342cde", "metadata": {"can_save": true, "citations": [], "code_blocks": {"0": {"edited": false, "id": "36pym9", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "1": {"edited": false, "id": "nxww09", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "10": {"edited": false, "id": "hm972l", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "11": {"edited": false, "id": "qbncya", "preview_language": null, "previewable": false}, "12": {"edited": false, "id": "kcvq8s", "preview_language": null, "previewable"