plementation pass.\n\nThe only thing still requiring your physical participation is the live **mic OFF → ON timing test**, but Nico does **not** need that to fix the structural failure Luce already proved: VoiceBridge has no device-loss recovery, its supervisor trusts a stale `_running` flag, and websocket failure can leave the bridge logically “running” but deaf. fileciteturn1file0L103-L122 fileciteturn1file0L147-L156\n\nGive Nico this update:\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" id=\"38426\" title=\"Nico — VoiceBridge Runtime Reliability Update\"}\n# GCE VOICEBRIDGE — NICO RUNTIME RELIABILITY FIX UPDATE\n\n**AUTHORITY:** Don  \n**SEAT:** Nico  \n**SOURCE:** Luce Runtime Health Recon  \n**MODE:** SURGICAL IMPLEMENTATION  \n**PRIORITY:** HIGH\n\n## DON COMMAND CORRECTION\n\nCanonical VoiceBridge pause/resume language is now:\n\n```text\nsleep\n→ pause\n\nwake up\n→ resume\n```\n\nThese must be **exact whole-utterance matches** after normal punctuation/case normalization.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nSleep.\n→ PAUSE\n\nI need to sleep.\n→ DICTATION\n\nWake up.\n→ RESUME\n\nI need to wake up early.\n→ DICTATION\n```\n\nRemove `stop listening` / `start listening` as active pause/resume commands.\n\nDo not modify other command-routing behavior.\n\n---\n\n# CURRENT VERIFIED FAILURES\n\nLuce established the following current-state defects.\n\n## 1. MIC OFF → ON DOES NOT RECOVER\n\nCurrent microphone config is:\n\n```text\nmic_device = default\n```\n\nwhich becomes:\n\n```python\ndevice=None\n```\n\nfor `sounddevice.RawInputStream`.\n\nPortAudio resolves the Windows default endpoint only when the stream opens.\n\nIf the USB mic is powered off:\n\n```text\nmic disappears\n→ callback stops / stream becomes unusable\n→ VoiceBridge _running flag remains True\n→ supervisor believes capture is healthy\n→ stream is never rebuilt\n→ VoiceBridge remains permanently deaf\n```\n\nCurrent recovery is effectively manual reconnect or process restart.\n\n### REQUIRED FIX\n\nAdd real microphone/capture liveness detection.\n\nThe system must detect when the active input stream has failed or stopped producing valid audio and transition capture into an unhealthy state.\n\nThe supervisor must then be able to:\n\n```text\ndetect failure\n→ close stale stream\n→ re-enumerate/re-resolve input\n→ reopen capture\n→ resume AssemblyAI audio flow\n```\n\nDo not depend solely on `_running == True`.\n\n---\n\n# 2. WINDOWS DEVICE RE-ENUMERATION\n\nLuce verified Windows currently exposes multiple historical instances of the same physical USB microphone.\n\nExamples include:\n\n```text\nMicrophone (5- USB PnP Audio Device)\nMicrophone (3- USB PnP Audio Device)\nMicrophone (2- USB PnP Audio Device)\n```\n\nand PortAudio exposes additional representations across:\n\n```text\nMME\nDirectSound\nWASAPI\nWDM-KS\n```\n\nDo not attempt to clean Windows devices in this implementation pass.\n\nInstead make VoiceBridge resilient to device disappearance/reappearance.\n\nAt reconnect time, re-resolve the configured/default input rather than retaining the dead stream.\n\n---\n\n# 3. SUPERVISOR MUST CHECK REAL HEALTH\n\nCurrent supervisor primarily checks:\n\n```python\ncapture.is_running()\n```\n\nbut this is only a Boolean state flag.\n\nLuce verified multiple workers can die while `_running` remains true.\n\nUpdate health supervision so that runtime health reflects actual component liveness.\n\nAt minimum consider:\n\n```text\naudio stream active\ncapture callback/activity heartbeat\nsend loop alive\nrecv loop alive\nAssemblyAI websocket alive\ncapture thread alive\ndispatcher alive\n```\n\nThe exact implementation is Nico's decision, but **process alive ≠ VoiceBridge healthy**.\n\nAvoid building an unnecessarily complex monitoring framework.\n\nUse the smallest dependable health signals available in the existing architecture.\n\n---\n\n# 4. ASSEMBLYAI WEBSOCKET RECOVERY\n\nLuce verified:\n\n```text\n_recv_loop can terminate on websocket close\n+\n_running may remain True\n+\nsupervisor therefore does not reconnect\n```\n\nCorrect this lifecycle.\n\nA closed/failed send or receive loop must cause capture/session health to become unhealthy.\n\nThe supervisor must then perform the normal reconnect path.\n\nDo not change:\n\n```text\nAssemblyAI model\nprovider\nkeyterms\naudio sample rate\n```\n\nas part of this slice.\n\n---\n\n# 5. OBSERVABILITY FIX\n\nCurrent logging cannot reliably diagnose runtime deaths.\n\nLuce verified `logging.basicConfig()` is not being activated in the normal runtime path, leaving important INFO-level events invisible.\n\nCritical events currently hidden include:\n\n```text\ncapture started\nAssemblyAI websocket closed\nsession terminated\ncapture pause/resume\n```\n\nCorrect logging initialization.\n\nRequired qualities:\n\n```text\ntimestamps\nlog level\ncomponent/logger name\nuseful lifecycle events\nexceptions with traceback where appropriate\n```\n\nAt minimum log:\n\n```text\nVoiceBridge start\nmic/device selected\ncapture stream opened\ncapture stream lost\ncapture stream reopened\nAssemblyAI connected\nAssemblyAI disconnected\nsend loop failure\nrecv loop failure\nsupervisor recovery attempt\nsupervisor recovery success/failure\npause\nresume\nshutdown\n```\n\nDo not create excessive per-audio-chunk logging.\n\n---\n\n# 6. DO NOT TOUCH VAD YET\n\nCurrent values include:\n\n```text\nvad_threshold = 500\nvad_silence_seconds = 3\n```\n\nLuce found possible VAD-related drop paths, but Don's live speech level has not yet been measured against the threshold.\n\nTherefore:\n\n**Do not change the VAD threshold or behavior in this implementation slice.**\n\nPreserve it for a later evidence-based test.\n\n---\n\n# 7. DO NOT REDESIGN FINALIZATION YET\n\nLuce also found potential loss around:\n\n```text\nend_of_turn\nturn_is_formatted\nForceEndpoint\n```\n\nThose are legitimate findings but are not yet sufficiently isolated.\n\nDo not change transcript-finalization semantics in this pass unless required to make runtime recovery safe.\n\nKeep this work focused.\n\n---\n\n# 8. IMPLEMENTATION ORDER\n\nExecute in this order:\n\n```text\n1. sleep / wake up command correction\n2. logging/observability\n3. real capture health detection\n4. microphone stream recovery\n5. websocket/send/recv health propagation\n6. supervisor reconnect behavior\n7. automated tests\n8. controlled runtime test\n```\n\nEach step should remain reversible.\n\n---\n\n# 9. REQUIRED TESTS\n\n## COMMAND LANGUAGE\n\n```text\nSleep.\n→ pause\n\nsleep\n→ pause\n\nI need to sleep.\n→ dictation\n\nSleep is important.\n→ dictation\n\nWake up.\n→ resume\n\nwake up\n→ resume\n\nI need to wake up tomorrow.\n→ dictation\n\nstop listening\n→ dictation\n\nstart listening\n→ dictation\n```\n\n---\n\n## HEALTH STATE\n\nAdd test coverage proving:\n\n```text\ncapture healthy\n→ supervisor does nothing\n```\n\nand:\n\n```text\ncapture stream failed\n→ capture becomes unhealthy\n→ supervisor attempts recovery\n```\n\n---\n\n## WEBSOCKET FAILURE\n\nSimulate or unit-test:\n\n```text\nrecv loop closes unexpectedly\n→ health becomes unhealthy\n→ reconnect path eligible\n```\n\nand where practical:\n\n```text\nsend loop fails\n→ health becomes unhealthy\n```\n\n---\n\n## DEVICE RECOVERY\n\nWhere hardware-independent mocking is possible:\n\n```text\ndevice available\n→ stream opens\n\ndevice disappears\n→ stream marked unhealthy\n\ndevice available again\n→ stream rebuilt\n```\n\nDo not fake a successful physical hardware test if one cannot be performed automatically.\n\n---\n\n# 10. LIVE VERIFICATION\n\nAfter automated tests pass:\n\n1. launch a clean single VoiceBridge instance\n2. verify current microphone selection in logs\n3. verify normal dictation\n4. verify `sleep`\n5. verify `wake up`\n6. verify command-word dictation remains safe\n7. verify AssemblyAI connection lifecycle appears in logs\n\nFor the actual physical:\n\n```text\nMIC OFF\n→ MIC ON\n```\n\ntest, Don may be needed to toggle the microphone.\n\nIf so, stop at that verification gate and report:\n\n```text\nREADY FOR DON MIC POWER-CYCLE TEST\n```\n\nDo not claim the physical reconnect behavior is verified until it is actually tested.\n\n---\n\n# 11. PRESERVE WORKING BEHAVIOR\n\nDo not modify:\n\n```text\nAssemblyAI provider/model\ncommand collision fix\ntranscription corrections\nkeyboard typing path\nVAD settings\nUI\nTTS\nQueuePanel\nCockpit\ndependencies\nWindows audio configuration\n```\n\nunless an unexpected ground-vs-spec conflict makes a change unavoidable.\n\nIf so, report before widening scope.\n\n---\n\n# 12. REQUIRED NICO RETURN\n\nReturn:\n\n```text\nGCE VOICEBRIDGE — RUNTIME RELIABILITY FIX RETURN\n\n1. STATUS\n2. PRE-CHANGE STATE\n3. FILES CHANGED\n4. SLEEP / WAKE COMMAND RESULT\n5. LOGGING FIX\n6. CAPTURE HEALTH MODEL\n7. MIC RECOVERY IMPLEMENTATION\n8. WEBSOCKET RECOVERY IMPLEMENTATION\n9. SUPERVISOR CHANGES\n10. TESTS ADDED\n11. FULL TEST RESULTS\n12. LIVE RUNTIME RESULTS\n13. DON HARDWARE TEST REQUIRED?\n14. REMAINING KNOWN RISKS\n15. DIFF SUMMARY\n16. SAFE FOR LUCE RE-VERIFY\n```\n\nFinish with:\n\n```text\nNICO VERDICT\n\nSLEEP COMMAND:\n[PASS / FAIL]\n\nWAKE UP COMMAND:\n[PASS / FAIL]\n\nMIC FAILURE DETECTION:\n[PASS / FAIL]\n\nAUTO MIC RECOVERY:\n[PASS / FAIL / NEEDS LIVE DON TEST]\n\nWS FAILURE DETECTION:\n[PASS / FAIL]\n\nAUTO WS RECOVERY:\n[PASS / FAIL]\n\nREAL HEALTH SUPERVISION:\n[PASS / FAIL]\n\nLOGGING OBSERVABLE:\n[PASS / FAIL]\n\nVAD MODIFIED:\nNO\n\nFINALIZATION MODIFIED:\nNO / explain if unavoidable\n\nFULL TEST SUITE:\n<count + PASS/FAIL>\n\nSAFE FOR LUCE:\n[YES / NO]\n\nCONFIDENCE:\n<0-100%>\n```\n\n## STOP CONDITION\n\nDo not optimize VoiceBridge generally.\n\nDo not clean Windows audio devices.\n\nDo not tune VAD.\n\nDo not redesign transcription.\n\nFix **runtime liveness, automatic recovery, observability, and Don's approved sleep/wake command semantics**.\n\nThen stop and return for Luce verification.\n:::\n\nSo you can send Nico **that right now**. After he gets the software recovery in 