: {"metadata": {}, "name": null, "role": "assistant"}, "channel": "final", "content": {"content_type": "text", "parts": ["Yep. Since **optimization work already happened and something regressed**, Luce should **not fix anything yet**. First job is to reconstruct the current runtime, identify the last-known-good boundary, and isolate exactly which optimization changed behavior.\n\nGive Luce this:\n\n:::writing{variant=\"document\" id=\"58321\" title=\"Luce — GCE VoiceBridge Breakage Recon\"}\n# GCE VOICEBRIDGE — BREAKAGE / REGRESSION RECON\n\n**DATE:** 2026-09-24  \n**AUTHORITY:** Don  \n**SEAT:** Luce — Verification / Ground Truth  \n**MODE:** READ-ONLY RECONNAISSANCE  \n**WORKSTREAM:** GCE Stack → VoiceBridge  \n**PURPOSE:** Determine what changed during recent VoiceBridge optimization work, identify what is actually broken, and establish a verified recovery boundary before Nico or another implementation seat touches the system.\n\n---\n\n## 0. PRIME DIRECTIVE\n\n**DO NOT FIX ANYTHING.**\n\nThis pass is diagnostic only.\n\nDo **not**:\n\n- rewrite code\n- refactor\n- reinstall packages\n- update dependencies\n- change environment variables\n- regenerate configuration\n- move or rename files\n- delete stale-looking files\n- restart services unless needed purely for non-destructive observation\n- modify startup configuration\n- normalize the architecture\n- assume an older implementation is obsolete\n- promote documentation over executable reality\n\nIf a fix appears obvious, document it under **PROPOSED CORRECTION** but do not apply it.\n\nWe need **ground truth before intervention**.\n\n---\n\n# 1. MISSION\n\nVoiceBridge has recently undergone optimization work.\n\nPrior to / during that work, VoiceBridge included a combination of:\n\n- voice/audio capture\n- speech-to-text\n- transcription-provider plumbing\n- proofreading / transcript cleanup\n- intent interpretation or command audit\n- routing\n- terminal / developer workflow integration\n- possible wake-word / execution behavior\n- local services or daemons\n- supporting scripts/configuration\n- provider/environment configuration\n\nSome recent optimization appears to have introduced a regression.\n\nYour job is to answer:\n\n> **What is VoiceBridge today, what changed, what is broken, and what is the smallest verified boundary around the regression?**\n\nDo not begin from architectural assumptions.\n\nBegin from the filesystem, executable code, configuration, logs, version history, and reproducible runtime behavior.\n\n---\n\n# 2. AUTHORITY RULES\n\nUse this evidence precedence:\n\n1. current executable/runtime behavior\n2. current source code\n3. current configuration actually consumed by runtime\n4. Git history / filesystem history / dated backups\n5. current project documentation\n6. accepted handoffs\n7. historical documentation\n8. chat discussion\n9. inference\n\nIf sources disagree, **report the disagreement**.\n\nDo not silently reconcile it.\n\nMark unresolved findings:\n\n`UNKNOWN / NEEDS RECONCILIATION`\n\n---\n\n# 3. LOCATE THE ESTATE\n\nFirst determine where the live VoiceBridge implementation actually resides.\n\nSearch likely GCE project/root locations for:\n\n```text\nVoiceBridge\nVoice_Bridge\nvoicebridge\nvoice_bridge\nvoice\nwhisper\ndeepgram\nassembly\nassemblyai\nspeech\ntranscript\nproofread\nintent\naudio\nmicrophone\nwake\nterminal\nbridge\n```\n\nIdentify:\n\n- live project root\n- duplicate project roots\n- archived copies\n- backup copies\n- test/sandbox copies\n- scripts outside the apparent project root\n- startup scripts pointing into other directories\n- services pointing into other directories\n- configuration outside the source tree\n\nReturn a concise filesystem map.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nVOICEBRIDGE ESTATE\n\nLIVE CANDIDATE:\nC:\\...\\VoiceBridge\n\nOTHER COPIES:\nC:\\...\\archive\\...\nC:\\...\\backup\\...\n...\n\nEXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES / CONFIG:\n.env\nPowerShell startup\nscheduled task\nservice\nregistry\nAppData\netc.\n```\n\nDo **not** decide which copy is authoritative until runtime evidence supports it.\n\n---\n\n# 4. ESTABLISH CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION\n\nDetermine the current technical stack.\n\nReport what you can verify for:\n\n## Audio ingestion\n\n- microphone library/API\n- recording lifecycle\n- sample rate\n- channels\n- buffering\n- silence detection\n- VAD\n- push-to-talk / continuous mode\n- audio format\n- temporary-file behavior\n\n## Speech-to-text\n\nIdentify all providers present in code/configuration.\n\nExamples may include, but are not limited to:\n\n- Whisper\n- OpenAI\n- Deepgram\n- AssemblyAI\n- local models\n- Windows speech services\n- other APIs\n\nFor each provider classify:\n\n```text\nACTIVE\nFALLBACK\nDEAD CODE\nEXPERIMENTAL\nUNKNOWN\n```\n\nDo not classify merely from filenames.\n\nTrace actual imports/config/runtime selection.\n\n## Transcript processing\n\nDetermine whether the transcript passes through:\n\n- normalization\n- proofreading\n- punctuation\n- spell correction\n- LLM cleanup\n- hallucination correction\n- confidence filtering\n- duplicate suppression\n- intent audit\n\nDocument the exact sequence.\n\n## Routing / execution\n\nTrace:\n\n```text\nMIC\n↓\nAUDIO CAPTURE\n↓\nSTT\n↓\nTRANSCRIPT\n↓\nCLEANUP / PROOFREAD\n↓\nINTENT / AUDIT\n↓\nROUTER\n↓\nDESTINATION / TERMINAL / APP\n```\n\nReplace that generic flow with the **actual current implementation**.\n\n---\n\n# 5. BUILD THE CURRENT RUNTIME GRAPH\n\nReturn an explicit runtime chain.\n\nExample only:\n\n```text\nInput Device\n    ↓\ncapture.py\n    ↓\nDeepgram websocket\n    ↓\ntranscript_processor.py\n    ↓\nproofreader\n    ↓\nintent_router.py\n    ↓\nterminal_bridge.ps1\n    ↓\nactive terminal\n```\n\nFor every node include:\n\n```text\nFILE:\nFUNCTION / CLASS:\nINPUT:\nOUTPUT:\nCALLED BY:\nCALLS:\nACTIVE?:\nEVIDENCE:\n```\n\nWe want the execution graph, not merely a folder inventory.\n\n---\n\n# 6. IDENTIFY RECENT CHANGES\n\nInspect available change evidence.\n\nUse, where available:\n\n- Git log\n- Git diff\n- Git status\n- file modification timestamps\n- backup copies\n- `_old`\n- `_bak`\n- `_working`\n- `_stable`\n- dated files\n- handoff documents\n- optimization notes\n- logs\n\nFocus particularly on recent optimization work.\n\nCreate:\n\n```text\nRECENT CHANGE LEDGER\n```\n\nwith:\n\n| Time / Commit | File | Change | Runtime Area | Risk | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\nPrioritize changes affecting:\n\n- audio capture\n- async behavior\n- queues\n- threads\n- websockets\n- buffering\n- VAD\n- provider swapping\n- model selection\n- transcript timing\n- cleanup\n- deduplication\n- event handlers\n- terminal focus\n- hotkeys\n- process lifecycle\n- environment loading\n- retry behavior\n- timeout behavior\n- startup scripts\n\n---\n\n# 7. FIND LAST-KNOWN-GOOD BOUNDARY\n\nDo not assume the newest code is the best code.\n\nLook for the most recent state where evidence indicates VoiceBridge was working correctly.\n\nReturn:\n\n```text\nLAST KNOWN GOOD\n\nDATE/TIME:\nCOMMIT / FILE STATE:\nEVIDENCE:\nWHAT WAS WORKING:\nWHAT WAS NOT YET IMPLEMENTED:\nCONFIDENCE:\n```\n\nIf there is no defensible last-known-good state:\n\n```text\nLAST KNOWN GOOD: UNKNOWN\n```\n\nDo not manufacture one.\n\n---\n\n# 8. REPRODUCE THE BREAKAGE\n\nAttempt to reproduce current behavior **without modifying the system**.\n\nDocument:\n\n```text\nTEST:\nEXPECTED:\nACTUAL:\nPASS / FAIL:\nERROR:\nLOG:\nTIMESTAMP:\n```\n\nTest the pipeline in increasingly complete slices where possible:\n\n### Test A — audio capture only\n\nCan audio be acquired reliably?\n\n### Test B — STT only\n\nCan known audio become a valid transcript?\n\n### Test C — transcript processor\n\nDoes known text survive cleanup correctly?\n\n### Test D — routing\n\nCan known text reach its intended routing target?\n\n### Test E — complete VoiceBridge\n\nCan:\n\n```text\nspeech → transcript → cleanup → route\n```\n\ncomplete successfully?\n\nThis is intended to locate the earliest failing boundary.\n\n---\n\n# 9. LATENCY / OPTIMIZATION RECON\n\nBecause the regression appeared during optimization, determine what was being optimized.\n\nInspect for changes intended to reduce:\n\n- transcription latency\n- startup latency\n- model latency\n- audio buffer delay\n- silence timeout\n- provider turnaround\n- proofreading latency\n- routing latency\n- terminal injection delay\n- token/API usage\n- CPU load\n- memory usage\n\nFor each optimization, report:\n\n```text\nOPTIMIZATION:\nOLD BEHAVIOR:\nNEW BEHAVIOR:\nINTENDED BENEFIT:\nOBSERVED SIDE EFFECT:\nREGRESSION RISK:\nEVIDENCE:\n```\n\nPay particular attention to optimization that changed **timing or state**, because these can produce behavior that appears random.\n\nExamples:\n\n- reduced buffer size\n- shorter silence threshold\n- concurrent transcript processing\n- async event handling\n- cancellation\n- aggressive debounce\n- dedupe windows\n- partial-transcript handling\n- connection reuse\n- provider failover\n- caching\n- premature cleanup\n- terminal focus changes\n\n---\n\n# 10. CONFIGURATION / ENVIRONMENT AUDIT\n\nInventory all configuration that can materially affect VoiceBridge.\n\nDo **not expose secret values**.\n\nReport only variable names and presence/state.\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nOPENAI_API_KEY = PRESENT\nDEEPGRAM_API_KEY = PRESENT\nASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY = ABSENT\nVOICE_PROVIDER = deepgram\n...\n```\n\nDetermine:\n\n- which `.env` is loaded\n- load order\n- duplicate `.env` files\n- provider-selection variables\n- model variables\n- audio-device variables\n- timeout variables\n- debug flags\n- feature flags\n- terminal destination config\n\nCheck for config drift between shell/runtime environments.\n\n---\n\n# 11. DEPENDENCY AUDIT\n\nCapture current relevant versions.\n\nExamples:\n\n```text\nPython / Node version\naudio libraries\nwebsocket libraries\nSTT SDKs\nOpenAI SDK\nDeepgram SDK\nAssemblyAI SDK\ndotenv/config loaders\nkeyboard/input libraries\nterminal integration dependencies\n```\n\nDetermine whether